# 48433 Software Architecture — Assignment 2  
## Architecture and Quality Plan for the Campus Library Reservation System

## 1. Context and scope

The Campus Library Reservation System (CLRS) replaces the existing study-room reservation tool across three university libraries. Students and staff must be able to search rooms and equipment, create and manage reservations, and receive reminders. Library staff must manage rooms, opening hours and block bookings, while kiosks display the current and next reservation for each room. The system integrates with SAML identity services, facilities-calendar iCal feeds and a read-only PostgreSQL room-inventory database.

This design covers the first release and the functional requirements FR-1 to FR-6:

- searching for rooms by campus, capacity, equipment and time;
- creating, modifying and cancelling reservations;
- staff-created recurring block bookings with 48 hours’ notice;
- kiosk updates within 10 seconds of reservation changes;
- email or push reminders 15 minutes before reservations;
- monthly utilisation reports by campus.

The principal quality requirements are availability, performance, security, modifiability, testability and operability. The proposed design is a **hexagonal architecture implemented as a modular monolith**, with an asynchronous event mechanism for kiosk updates, notifications and reporting
